{% doc %}
  blocks/_article-read-more.liquid — private.

  The card's call to action, through `snippets/button.liquid`.

  ## Nothing about the button is reimplemented here

  Variant, size, icon, badge, width and the hover effect are all the snippet's,
  so this block is a label, a destination and a pass-through. A read-more that
  drew its own anchor would be a second button in the theme, with a second set
  of hover states to keep in step with Theme settings › Buttons.

  ## It is a second link to the same place, and that is on purpose

  The title above already links to the article and `base.css` stretches it over
  the whole card. This one is the visible affordance — the thing a customer
  looks for and clicks. Two links to one destination is only a problem when the
  second announces nothing: the label is real text, so a screen reader user gets
  "Read more, link" and the title link separately, which is the same choice
  `snippets/article-card.liquid` makes on the blog index.

  It raises itself above the stretched title link in `base.css`, or the card-wide
  overlay would swallow the click that lands on it.
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign article = closest.article
  assign s = block.settings

  assign label = s.label
  if label == blank
    assign label = 'blogs.article.read_more' | t
  endif

  assign icon = s.icon | default: 'arrow-right'
-%}

{%- capture button_style -%}
  {%- render 'spacing', block: s, declarations: true -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- if article -%}
  <div
    class="article-read-more"
    data-block-spacing
    style="{{ button_style | strip_newlines | strip }}"
    {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
  >
    {% render 'button',
       label: label,
       href: article.url,
       variant: s.variant,
       size: s.size,
       icon: icon,
       icon_position: s.icon_position,
       icon_style: s.icon_style,
       width: s.width,
       class: 'article-read-more__button' %}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

